# Multi-Agent Collaboration Guidelines

## Concurrent Work Awareness

Multiple AI agents may be working in this workspace simultaneously. Keep this in mind when making changes.

## Atomic Commits

- Commit changes atomically - each commit should be a complete, self-contained change
- Don't leave the codebase in a broken state between commits
- Prefer smaller, focused commits over large sweeping changes
- Complete one logical unit of work before committing

## Handling Concurrent Changes

- If you encounter unexpected changes in files you're working on, don't panic - another agent may have made them
- If git operations fail due to conflicts or changed state, assess the situation calmly:
  - Pull/fetch to see what changed
  - Determine if your changes are still relevant
  - Rebase or merge as appropriate
- Don't assume unexpected file changes are errors - verify before "fixing" them

## Best Practices

- Read files fresh before making edits when possible, especially after any delays
- Keep file edits minimal and focused to reduce conflict potential
- If you notice files have changed since you last read them, re-read before proceeding
- Communicate clearly about what you're changing and why in commit messages
